rley root epidermis</article-title><source>Planta</source><year>2007</year><volume>225</volume><fpage>753</fpage><lpage>761</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16955270</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davenport</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tester</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A weakly voltage-dependent, nonselective cation channel mediates toxic sodium influx in wheat</article-title><source>Plant Physiology</source><year>2000</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>823</fpage><lpage>834</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10712546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dvo&#x00159;&#x000e1;k</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gorham</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Methodology of gene-transfer by homoeologous recombination into <italic>Triticum turgidum</italic>: transfer of K<sup>+</sup>/Na<sup>+</sup> discrimination from <italic>Triticum aestivum</italic></article-title><source>Genome</source><year>1992</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>639</fpage><lpage>646</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dvo&#x00159;&#x000e1;k</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Noaman</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Goyal</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gorham</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Enhancement of the salt tolerance of <italic>Triticum turgidum</italic> L. by the <italic>Kna</italic>1 locus transferred from the <italic>Triticum aestivum</italic> L. chromosome 4D by homoeologous recombination</article-title><source>Theoretical and Applied Genetics</source><year